{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11073-the-principle-and-the-god-machine","id":11073,"title":"The Principle and the God-Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T22:56:53-08:00","id":11073,"title":"The Principle and the God-Machine","content":"With things firmly established that the two entities are seperate things, how do we fall? The general theory is vaguely Gnostic (with Principle as Creator and Machine as Demiurge) and that the Machine is a force of stasis competing against the Principle, a force for change and creation. What role does Pyros serve on a metaphysical level, if Essence is the natural mystic energy of the world? Why do I feel like the God-Machinew as called The Purpose somewhere? Can a qashmallim Fall? All these questions and more, (hopefully) answered here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:01:53-08:00","id":11076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11073-the-principle-and-the-god-machine#post11073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do I feel like the God-Machinew as called The Purpose somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I can answer. That'd be because the artifact letters in the God-Machine Chronicle book present an angel leading people through the innards of the God-Machine, making the &quot;It is the Purpose&quot; quote a la &quot;it is the Principle,&quot; and offering a demiurge an artifact to be used in catalyzing the creation of a Promethean.<br /> <br /> They also tie into the head-rack from Ten Photographs in the Horror Recognition Guide. Overall, not a bad story but it tries to tie together things I feel are best left separate. Wood's got to let up on using the head-rack in my opinion, it was brilliant the first time but it really doesn't withstand being repeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:06:01-08:00","id":11077,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure a <i>qashmal</i> can &quot;fall&quot; like an angel can. After all, while they're born for their missions, the Principle seems to have an easier time creating them than the God-Machine has creating Angels. If the Principle needs a <i>qashmal</i>, it seems like all it needs to do is focus Pyros or Flux in the proper fashion. As for what Pyros is metaphysically, it's probably the equivalent of refined radioactive materials to Essence's kerosene. Neither of them can really fuel what the other is capable of fueling. The fact that Pyros seems to be so far removed from all the other &quot;supernatural fuels&quot;... I mean, from what I can tell, you can't create it with Mana, I doubt you can make it with Glamour (although it and Glamour are probably fairly close to one another, metaphysically speaking), Plasm and Vitae can't convert to it... So yeah.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say that the scale is Essence -&gt; Aether -&gt; Plasm -&gt; Vitae -&gt; Mana -&gt; Possible Future Line Intermediary -&gt; Glamour -&gt; Possible Future Line Intermediaries -&gt; Pyros","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:13:20-08:00","id":11615,"title":"","content":"Per Dave Brookshaw, <i>qashmallim</i> cannot Fall. My personal theory is that if the Unchained are right about the <i>qashmallim</i>, then they\u2019re <i>already</i> \u201cfallen\u201d, in that they\u2019re former servants of the God-Machine. They differ from the Unchained because they\u2019ve signed on with a new master (the Principle) instead of becoming independent agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:22:29-08:00","id":11714,"title":"","content":"I posted something similar to this concept in the Promethean threads prior to the Kickstarter preview release, so it makes me really happy they're actually gonna touch on this a bit with Demon.<br /> <br /> Regarding personal theories:<br /> <br /> What if instead; a <i>qashmal</i> isn't already &quot;fallen&quot; per se, but more they are agents of the Fall itself. That doesn't make them Demons or even agents of the God-Machine either, but instead an essential process outside of the Machine's purview.<br /> <br /> As an example; an Angel is on a mission, yet unknowingly is an asset for a <i>qashmal</i> with a mission to cause an Angel to fall. If successful, the new Demon would never interact with that particular <i>qashmal</i> which caused it cause its mission was essentially over and so goes back to the Principle.<br /> <br /> Angels (likely Arch-Angels) possibly might be given missions as well, to capture a <i>qashmal</i> for re-purposing, in the similar way they grab other raw materials for occult matrices.<br /> <br /> A 3rd possible outcome would be joint missions; where the Divine Fire &amp; the God-Machine's interests are conceptually aligned. The difference between the Principle and the Purpose would essentially be similar to conflicts between Agents within NSA (US) and MI5 (UK). Maybe some initial fighting in the confusion but eventually gets cleared up from a call upstairs with new intel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T22:31:06-08:00","id":11900,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the God-Machine is about keeping the status quo, who the Principle is about evolution. The God-Machine is keeping the world together, while the Principle is trying to uplift it. Whether or not that they are always in contention, sometimes in contention, or in perfect, if inscrutable, harmony is probably a good source for chronicle-building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:21:22-08:00","id":15919,"title":"","content":"Here is my personal pet theory: <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The God-Machine and the Principle are kind of the same thing, but at different times. The Principle represents the force of creation itself; it is the state of the God-Machine at the beginning of time, when the (physical) universe has been created by it; or even uncountable versions of the universe. Since then, the God-Machine developed over aeons to its current state on earth, as we know it now. Since time is obviously a bendable thing for the God-Machine, the Principle still has some influence over the world and interacts with its current form, the God-Machine, in a weird and unknowable manner.<br /> <br /> This would explain the connection between Pyros and Essence in the following way: Pyros is the pure and raw energy of creation. Essence is a more impure, but further advanced energy form the God-Machine useses nowadays. Think of it like iron and steel: although steel is 'polluted' with other elements, it is a more versatile and handable construction material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T17:44:17-08:00","id":16884,"title":"","content":"See, I think of Pyros and Essence in a different way. I see Essence as being like gasoline. There's a lot of things that are very different that run on it (last I figured, a generator was a very different machine from a lawnmower was very different machine from a car), and it's a basic source of a good amount of power. Pyros, on the other hand, is like U-235. It's an incredibly potent source of energy, but you <i>really</i> have to handle it with care, and you pretty much have to build a specialized device to even use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:53:00-08:00","id":17000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11073-the-principle-and-the-god-machine?p=11615#post11615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Dave Brookshaw, <i>qashmallim</i> cannot Fall. My personal theory is that if the Unchained are right about the <i>qashmallim</i>, then they\u2019re <i>already</i> \u201cfallen\u201d, in that they\u2019re former servants of the God-Machine. They differ from the Unchained because they\u2019ve signed on with a new master (the Principle) instead of becoming independent agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, The Unchained have free will. The Qashmallim seem to lack that. All they can work on is their mission and don't have the ability for self-actualization.<br /> <br /> In a way, The Qashmallim seem to be a more elemental versions of angels. Serving the mission is not only what they do but also what they are while the Unchained have the ability to go beyond their mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T04:29:21-08:00","id":17074,"title":"","content":"While not a bad idea, the stasis-creation duality seems to contradict GMC pretty hard. Whatever else the God-Machine is, it certainly doesn't seem to mind radically oveturning the world if it fits with it's plans.<br /> <br /> (I hadn't thought of the direct gnostic analogy of the principle as creator and God Machine as demiurge; that's pretty clever.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:38:09-08:00","id":17088,"title":"","content":"This stasis-creation duality is getting close to the Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld from oWoD. There isint a Wyrm equivalent now, is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:38:57-08:00","id":17230,"title":"","content":"Perhaps that's part of the problem. The Underworld is full of stuff the Wyrm should have eaten, and it's dragging the world down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:05:18-08:00","id":17294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11073-the-principle-and-the-god-machine?p=17088#post17088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stasis-creation duality is getting close to the Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld from oWoD. There isint a Wyrm equivalent now, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that the creation/preservation/destruction divide is <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trimurti\" target=\"_blank\">something with Actual Mythological Precedent</a> I feel that this argument rightly deserves to be barred from further use for its utter uselessness to the discussion.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths are <i>filled</i> with destroyer-beings. So, to a degree, is the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T11:58:14-08:00","id":17842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11073-the-principle-and-the-god-machine?p=17088#post17088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stasis-creation duality is getting close to the Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld from oWoD. There isint a Wyrm equivalent now, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Principle kinda acts as both; Elipidos (Creation) and Lilithim (Destruction) choirs work like the Pablo Picasso quote; &quot;<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Every </span></span><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>act of creation</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> is first an </span></span><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>act of destruction&quot;</b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}